{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7d0fb871-13fe-4c6c-8e74-5d7a68ba71bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "7d036524-878f-4f49-8c71-ad90cda08a88",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-- Python is a high level interpreted programming language\n",
    "-- It is easy to learn\n",
    "-- It has large no.of libraries which helps us to do complex work with very little code\n",
    "-- It is used in web development, DS, AI, Automation, Apps, Games - almost everyweher"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d4400a77-4ac0-4c7f-9f36-37ac8f7634a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Why Python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "bbe9462c-5d7a-4c82-9a92-d7dcdd9461ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Becoz python reduces our effort we can finish a task in 5 lines that may take 20 lines in other language like C, C++ or Java"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d84a4dc6-4d92-4d7c-b7c4-a40e2b150498",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Identifier"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "48bfea70-4e36-430e-8cc8-edce1ec8df1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Identifier is an any name we give in python \n",
    "ex: variable name, function name, class name, etc..\n",
    "realtime ex: Boy & Girl (names based on gender)\n",
    "\n",
    "Rules:\n",
    "1. Must start with A-Z, a-z, _ (underscore)\n",
    "2. Cannot start with numbers\n",
    "3. Cannot contain special symbols like : @, #, $, %, &, *, etc...\n",
    "4. Cannot use Keywords as identifiers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22886b75-faa5-41c3-b5f5-a15f27312ea4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Keywords"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "90c5a066-762c-48b8-be64-394ec7a0410a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Keywords are reserved words in python \n",
    "They already have a meaning, so we cannot use them as identifiers\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: if,for,while,class,return,break,True,False,etc..\n",
    "\n",
    "Python uses these words internally, so we are not allowed to change their purpose"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ba2f9789-8db4-4615-b1b9-6765bc20215f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Variable"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "1ec07605-ae3d-4026-ac1e-ab5d55a463ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Variable is a container where we store a value \n",
    "\n",
    "Ex: a = 10\n",
    "10 is a value stored inside a varaible called 'a'\n",
    "\n",
    "ex2: Think of a box with a label"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62b39532-f1cc-4586-b3aa-f3c2c0e58147",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Comments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "eede196b-a6e2-4a0f-8c74-38830d58a854",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Comments are notes written for humans, not the computer\n",
    "-- python will ignore comments\n",
    "-- we use them to explain code\n",
    "\n",
    "Types of comments\n",
    "1. Single line comments\n",
    "-- Starts with # \n",
    "\n",
    "ex: # hi hello \n",
    "\n",
    "2. Multi line comments\n",
    "-- uses triple quotes '''___''' or \"\"\"___\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: \"\"\" Good morning \"\"\"\n",
    "    ''' Good evening '''\n",
    "These are not real comments, But python treats them as strings not used anywhere\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Why ?\n",
    "-- To explain code\n",
    "-- For documentation\n",
    "-- For disabling code temporarily"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "deeafe2c-2f22-4608-9e62-7274d1e9a438",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Statement"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "bb420eb2-432f-419e-bf4e-6d0310b42221",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Statement is a complete instruction given to python \n",
    "\n",
    "--- Types of stmts ---\n",
    "\n",
    "1. single line stmt\n",
    "ex: a = 10+20+30   #SLS\n",
    "    a\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Multiple line stmt\n",
    "if stmt is too long, we can break it into multiple lines using a backslash (\\) -- tells python that this line continues below, don't end the stmt yet (joins all the lines into one single line)\n",
    "ex: b = 10+20+30\\\n",
    "        +40+50+\\\n",
    "        60+70+80\n",
    "    b\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Assignment Statement\n",
    "Used to store values in variables\n",
    "ex:\n",
    "name = \"Keerty\"\n",
    "dept = \"DS\"\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Print Statement\n",
    "Used to display output.\n",
    "ex:\n",
    "print(\"Welcome to Python\")\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Conditional Statement\n",
    "Used for decision making.\n",
    "ex:\n",
    "if age >= 18:\n",
    "   print(\"Eligible to vote\")\n",
    "\n",
    "6.Loop Statement\n",
    "Used to repeat actions.\n",
    "ex:\n",
    "for i in range(3):\n",
    "   print(i)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0b88c1db-89b4-46a5-8320-b81fae4f30ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Variable assignment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "af363186-e7a2-4b2f-a112-7fc99a0792d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Variable assignment means storing a value inside a variable using '=' symbol\n",
    "ex: x = 10\n",
    "    y = 5\n",
    "\n",
    "Here, X is a variable\n",
    "      = is an assignment operator\n",
    "      10 is a value assigned"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "59b5569d-e3cb-43fa-b9c3-d612ff924d47",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Multiple Variable Assignment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "3bb2cd40-3802-475f-acb3-13ccef161098",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Python allows assigning values in different styles\n",
    "1. Multiple variables, Multiple values\n",
    "ex: a,b,c = 10,20,30\n",
    "    print(a,b,c)    \n",
    "each variable gets the value in order\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Multiple variables, same value\n",
    "-- all variables get the same value\n",
    "ex: x=y=z=100\n",
    "    print(x,y,z)\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Swapping variable (without Temp variable)\n",
    "-- python special feature\n",
    "-- no need of third variable like in other language (c,c++,java)\n",
    "ex: a = 5\n",
    "    b = 10\n",
    "    a,b = b,a\n",
    "    print(a,b)  # 10,5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b537b1e-7b09-4706-bb22-9691dba6c90f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Data Types"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "371859cb-7f89-4762-96c9-343e43b42d2f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "what type of value a variable is holding\n",
    "\n",
    "Types of Data Types\n",
    "1. Numeric -- Numbers\n",
    "a. Integer (whole nos -- no decimals)\n",
    "-- defined as int\n",
    "ex: a = 19\n",
    "b. Float (nos with decimal)\n",
    "-- defined as float\n",
    "ex: a = 9.03\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Boolean -- stores Truth Values (True/False)\n",
    "-- defined as bool\n",
    "ex: b = True\n",
    "    c = False\n",
    "\n",
    "3. String -- a seq of characters put inside a single/double/triple quotes\n",
    "-- defined as str\n",
    "ex : name = 'Keerty'\n",
    "     dept = \"DS\"\n",
    "     city = '''Hyd'''"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3c3272e9-cdf1-484d-acb6-3d5fc67605d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# String indexing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "b6e4aad5-cce2-4609-82d5-8c55bbb08b3c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In String each character has a position (index)\n",
    "-- String indexing means accessing a character by using its position\n",
    "\n",
    "Types of SI\n",
    "1. Positive SI (L to R) -- starts from 0 \n",
    "2. Negative SI (R to L) -- starts from -1\n",
    "\n",
    "syntax : Var_name[index no.]\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: s = 'Hello Python'\n",
    "    s[5] , s[-3], s[0]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d0f39814-07ab-47db-8617-3543c90672d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# String Slicing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "be2f5c88-b859-4c3c-a5dc-69c512de693f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "String Slicing\n",
    "means taking a piece of string \n",
    "-- here we're aiming to cut the string\n",
    "\n",
    "Syntax : var_name[start:stop:step]\n",
    "                  included : excluded(stop-1) : jumpvalue (default = 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: s = \"Python Programming\"\n",
    "\n",
    "s[0:6] #=Python\n",
    "s[0:15:2] #every 2nd char\n",
    "s[::-1] # reverse string"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ae162f9a-7f52-4d69-9f9f-786a3a0886b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Type Casting"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "ad18fbb3-5f64-4e4b-b8f8-2584867e4520",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "simply means changing/converting one datatype into another datatype\n",
    "\n",
    "Types of TC\n",
    "1. Automatic TC (Implicit)\n",
    "-- Python itself converts the datatype when needed \n",
    "-- python interpreter based on some hierarchy\n",
    "Float -- int -- bool\n",
    "-- stings are not involved in ATC\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: a = 2+3.4+True  # True = 1\n",
    "    a  # float value u will get\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Forced TC (Explict)/ Manual TC\n",
    "-- we use python fns (Built-in classes) to convert the value into our required DT\n",
    "The Main Fns are : \n",
    "a. int() -- convert any type of data into Integer\n",
    "b. float() -- convert any type of data into Float\n",
    "c. str() -- convert any type of data into String\n",
    "d. bool() -- convert any type of data into Boolean\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: int -- float\n",
    "    a = 10\n",
    "    a\n",
    "    b = float(a)\n",
    "    b"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ccbc91eb-deb1-4748-bb5e-3ba7d07c8974",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# OPERATORS "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "9a2e971c-0a14-4477-8956-bf73a1890728",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "are ntg but special symbols that help python perform actions on variables/values\n",
    "\n",
    "1. ARTHIMETIC OPERATORS  \n",
    "-- these are the basic math operators we use for calculations\n",
    "a. addition +\n",
    "b. sub -\n",
    "c. mul *\n",
    "d. div /\n",
    "e. floor div // (gives only the whole no.)\n",
    "f. modulus % (gives reminder)\n",
    "g. exponent ** (power)\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: a = 10\n",
    "    b = 3\n",
    "    a+b , a-b, a*b, a/b, a%b, a**b\n",
    "\n",
    "2. COMPARISION OPERATOR\n",
    "-- these operators compares 2 values/variables and returns True/False as o/p\n",
    "1. == equal to \n",
    "2. != not equal to\n",
    "3. > greater than\n",
    "4. < less than\n",
    "5. >= greater than or equal to  \n",
    "6. <= less than or equal to\n",
    "\n",
    "3. LOGICAL OPERATORS\n",
    "these helps us to compare multiple conditions at a time\n",
    "-- it returns True/False\n",
    "1. AND -- TRUE only if both the conditions are TRUE\n",
    "2. OR -- TRUE even if any 1 condition is TRUE\n",
    "3. NOT -- reverse the output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0554bd98-ae15-4d07-9248-749e2c42cd12",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Conditional Statements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "cdbe5e5c-10be-442c-aa72-786777df8162",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Conditional Statements\n",
    "Operators only compare/calculate values\n",
    "but i want to make a decision based on those comparisions\n",
    "for that we use these conditional stmts\n",
    "\n",
    "Types of Conditional Stmts\n",
    "1. If stmt\n",
    "-- Executes a block of code only if the condition is TRUE\n",
    "syntax: if condition:\n",
    "           stmt\n",
    "-- indentation : 1Tab space/4 spaces \n",
    "\n",
    "ex: age = 20\n",
    "    if age>= 18:\n",
    "        print(\"Eligible\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex2: num = 10\n",
    "     if num>0:\n",
    "         print(\"+ve no.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex3: marks = 95\n",
    "     if marks == 95:\n",
    "         print(\"Great Score\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "42948c81-2061-4f29-9d67-d75259c86052",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "2. if else stmt\n",
    "-- if works only when the condition is TRUE but what if the condition is false?\n",
    "we need an alternative path -- that is else\n",
    "\n",
    "syntax: \n",
    "if condition:\n",
    "    stmt \n",
    "else:\n",
    "    stmt\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: \n",
    "num = 7\n",
    "if num % 2 == 0:\n",
    "    print(\"Even\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Odd\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex2:\n",
    "temp = 32\n",
    "if temp > 30:\n",
    "    print(\"Hotday\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Nrml day\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex3:\n",
    "a = 10\n",
    "b = 2\n",
    "if a>b:\n",
    "    print(\"A is big\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"B is big\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "25a59d8e-5ce5-4b63-a8fb-9513dc5883ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "input() fn : \n",
    "-- Till now we used fixed values but in real programs\n",
    "we want users to enter values, that's where input() comes in\n",
    "-- by default it returns string \n",
    "\n",
    "syntax:\n",
    "var = input(\"message\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex:\n",
    "name = input(\"Enter ur name:\")\n",
    "print(\"Hello\",name)\n",
    "\n",
    "ex1: \n",
    "age = int(input(\"Enter ur age:\"))\n",
    "print(\"I'm\",age,\"years old\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e2e927d9-1432-42fe-97cd-5a119e919e53",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3. elif stmt\n",
    "-- if else gives 2 choices but sometimes we need multiple choices\n",
    "not just True/False but many conditions \n",
    "that's where elif helps\n",
    "\n",
    "Syntax:\n",
    "if condition1:\n",
    "    stmt\n",
    "elif cond2:\n",
    "    stmt\n",
    "elif cond3:\n",
    "    stmt\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    stmt\n",
    "\n",
    "ex: \n",
    "marks = int(input(\"Enter a number:\"))\n",
    "if marks >= 90:\n",
    "    print(\"A grade\")\n",
    "elif marks >= 75:\n",
    "    print(\"B grade\")\n",
    "elif marks >= 60:\n",
    "    print(\"C grade\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"D grade\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex2:\n",
    "age = 45\n",
    "if age < 13:\n",
    "    print(\"Child\")\n",
    "elif age<20:\n",
    "    print(\"Teen\")\n",
    "elif age<60:\n",
    "    print(\"Adult\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Senior\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex3:\n",
    "day = 3\n",
    "if day == 1:\n",
    "    print(\"Monday\")\n",
    "elif day == 2:\n",
    "    print(\"Tuesday\")\n",
    "elif day == 7:\n",
    "    print(\"Sunday\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    Print(\"Invalid\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "478c3045-9ef1-4ae7-8058-b7ccbf8ec527",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "4. Nested if stmt\n",
    "-- sometimes one condition depends on another then we use it\n",
    "-- nested if is ntg but a decision inside another decision\n",
    "\n",
    "syntax:\n",
    "if cond1:\n",
    "    if cond2:\n",
    "        stmt\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        stmt\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    stmt\n",
    "\n",
    "ex:\n",
    "num = 12\n",
    "if num>0:\n",
    "    if num%2==0:\n",
    "        print(\"+ve even\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"+ve odd\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"-ve number\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ex2:\n",
    "num = int(input(\"Enter a num\"))\n",
    "if num>0:\n",
    "    if num%2==0:\n",
    "        print(\"+ve even\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"+ve odd\")\n",
    "if num<0:\n",
    "    if num%2 == 0:\n",
    "        print(\"-ve even\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"-ve odd\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ex3:\n",
    "score = 80\n",
    "if score >= 50:\n",
    "    if score >= 90:\n",
    "        print(\"Excellent\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"Good\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Fail\")"
   ]
  },
